{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "lib": ["ESNext", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"],
    "target": "ESNext",
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    "types": ["bun-types"],
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "strict": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true
  },
  /*
   * Why this file exists at all: `tsconfig.json` includes only ["src",
   * "../shared"], and CI runs these 122 suites with `bun test`, which strips
   * types without checking them. So nothing anywhere read the tests' types —
   * a suite could assert against a shape the module no longer has and stay
   * green until somebody read it.
   *
   * `types` REPLACES rather than adds, which is why this cannot be a second
   * `include` in the main config: the app is typed against `vite/client` and
   * the suites against `bun-types`, and one file cannot hold both. `mobile/`
   * hit the same wall first and split the same way — this mirrors
   * mobile/tsconfig.test.json deliberately.
   *
   * DOM is in `lib` because src/lib/ reaches for localStorage, window and
   * WebSocket, and bun-types does not describe them.
   */
  "include": [
    "test/**/*.ts",
    "src/lib/**/*.ts",
    "../shared/**/*.ts",
    "../server/src/pairing.ts"
  ]
}
